    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48626" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tot-jŭgus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		jugum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>so many</i> (Appuleian): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">totjugis diebus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 2, p. 125, 22</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sidera,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. de Deo Socr. p. 46</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">invitamenta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Flor. 4, p. 360, 3</span></i>
			.— Collat. form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">totjŭgis</span></b> , e: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">homo totjugi scientiā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Flor. 2, p. 346, 30</span></i>
			.</div>
